# The event log is append-only and line-oriented, so a union merge is literally its
# semantics: two developers working different epics each append their own transitions, and
# both sets are correct. Without this, every multi-developer merge conflicts on this file
# alone — measured 2026-10-11 on two clones working two epics: the state tree merged clean
# and this was the single conflict, which union reduced to none with all four events intact.
#
# It is the only state file that takes a merge driver. The others are deliberately left to
# conflict: issues.yaml allocates per-epic so disjoint owners never collide semantically,
# pm-calibration.yaml loses at worst a sample (degrading an estimate, never corrupting
# state), and adr-register.yaml is a global allocator whose answer is `adr-reserve --count`
# BEFORE the fork, not a merge strategy after it.
#
# Requires nothing of the user: `union` is built into git.
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/state/events.jsonl merge=union
**/state/events.jsonl                                   merge=union
